{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_fczo7ahnw77b5ydkd4ihumdnn6vaxiepsjbzpfd64ua4ughfkyba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The project is clean and the build succeeds. All `unimplemented!()` placeholders have been replaced with working pure-Rust implementations.\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C math library to safe, idiomatic Rust by implementing every function in `src/castom_math.rs`:\n\n- **`castom_abs`** — integer absolute value (using `wrapping_neg` to avoid `i32::MIN` panic, matching C two's-complement behavior).\n- **`castom_fabs`** — branch-based absolute value mirroring the C source.\n- **`castom_floor` / `castom_ceil`** — same `i64` cast trick as C, with NaN/overflow guards using Rust's `i64::MAX`/`i64::MIN` as `f64`.\n- **`castom_trunc`** — dispatches to `floor`/`ceil`.\n- **`castom_fmod`** — `x - trunc(x/y) * y` like the C version.\n- **`castom_sqrt`** — Newton's iteration; returns NaN for negative or NaN input, with an early return for `0.0` to avoid divide-by-zero in the iteration.\n- **`castom_exp`** — Taylor series accumulation with iteration cap to guard against runaway loops.\n- **`castom_log`** — port of the original (somewhat dense) reduction-and-series algorithm; returns +∞ for `x == 0` and NaN for negative input.\n- **`castom_pow`** — recursive structure with integer/fractional split, sign tracking, and edge cases for `0^x`, `x^0`, negative bases with non-integer exponents.\n- **`castom_sin` / `castom_cos`** — argument reduction by `2π` then Taylor series.\n- **`castom_tan`** — exact-match special cases (π/6, π/4, …) before falling back to `sin/cos`.\n- **`castom_asin`** — Maclaurin series for `|x|<1`, exact values at ±1, NaN otherwise.\n- **`castom_acos` / `castom_atan`** — derived from `asin` and `sqrt`, matching the C originals.\n- **`castom_factorial`** — iterative product (uses `wrapping_mul` to mirror C's unsigned overflow semantics).\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no remaining `unimplemented!()`/`todo!()`/`panic!()`. `cargo build` is clean and ad-hoc verification against `std::f64` math passes within `EPS_6` tolerance for all the cases exercised by the original C test suite."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":188,"cache_read_input_tokens":37332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":188,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76383556-2854-4d34-861c-dec9a9a07c5e","uuid":"8686c327-e4d9-41d5-b348-c75c0affec57"}
